cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Kimberling's inequality for Archimedean copulas: proof and Lean 4 formalization"
authors:
  - family-names: Kao
    given-names: Ming-Chih
    affiliation: Stanford University
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - copulas
  - Archimedean copula
  - complete monotonicity
  - Bernstein theorem
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  Proof, with a machine-checked Lean 4 formalization, that every bivariate Archimedean copula C with completely
  monotone inverse generator satisfies C(a,a) - a^2 >= C(u,v) - uv for a = (u+v)/2, answering MathOverflow question
  195959 (C. Kimberling, 2015). The formalization uses the Hausdorff-Bernstein-Widder theorem from the TauCeti library. A stronger, paper-only result shows that C - uv is Schur-concave for stochastically increasing strict Archimedean copulas.
references:
  - type: software
    title: TauCeti
    url: "https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti"
